diversion to unauthorized end uses, end users, or destinations.</p><p>Specifically, the bill directs the Department of Commerce's Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS) to establish the program for five years and station at least 20 export control officers at U.S. diplomatic or consular posts. The bill also&nbsp;outlines the duties of export control officers.</p><p>Additionally, BIS must appoint a director to lead the program.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-27T13:39:39Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Export Controls Enforcement Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:21:58Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:21:59Z"}
